{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,30p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc; sed -n '1,26p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/safepoint.cljc; sed -n '1,28p' src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint.cljc; sed -n '148,170p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/siteset.cljc; sed -n '1,32p' src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc; sed -n '1,32p' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.php.antlr.safepoint\n  \"The PHP `:loop` and `:call` hooks. A bounded run charges one safepoint to\n   its per-run counter; exhaustion unwinds past guest handlers and raises the\n   operational fatal, not a guest Throwable.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.core.module :as module]))\n\n\n(def profile\n  {:loop 'php.sp/loop, :call {:hook 'php.sp/call, :sequence true}})\n\n\n(def ticks-profile\n  \"Statement completion hooks for PHP's lexical ticks directives. This is\n   separate from the execution-budget profile so ticks do not charge it.\"\n  {:line {:hook 'php.sp/line, :operands true, :after true}})\n\n\n(def fatal-text\n  \"Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded\")\n\n\n(def ^:private function-definitions\n  '[[php.sp/exhaust!\n     ;; the terminal root escape: guest handlers, returns and finalizers\n     ;; cannot replace the operational fatal\n     (fn []\n       (php/root-fatal \"Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded\"))]\n    [php.sp/tick\n(ns yang.python.antlr.safepoint\n  \"The Python hook prelude for `yang.safepoint` (Architect safepoint\n   design, slice 1: signals; slice 2: recursion). Universal AST, like the\n   base prelude; the stage only places `(py.sp/loop)`, `(py.sp/call)` and\n   `(py.sp/return body)`, and what they mean is written here.\n\n   Signals. The composition hands the task a signal stream, a sealed\n   reference in the store under `signals-key`; a host adapter appends one\n   plain value per delivered signal. Each hook reads it with `stream/poll!`,\n   which answers `:dao.stream/blocked` rather than parking, so a program\n   with no signal pending never waits at a safepoint. On a signal (or a\n   gap: values were lost, so at least one arrived) the registered Python\n   handler is called with the signal and None, as CPython calls\n   `handler(signum, frame)`; with none registered, `KeyboardInterrupt` is\n   raised there, through `py/raise`: an explicit continuation invoke at an\n   explicit program point. Delivery is not journalled (owner decision 8).\n\n   Recursion (slice 2). Depth measures the current continuation: it is\n   `:base` plus `:depth` of the base prelude's dynamic-context record\n   `py.rt/ctx`, the one cell that also holds the handler stack (`:base` is\n   0 outside generators; each crossing into a generator sets it to the\n   resumer's absolute depth plus one). `py.sp/call`, at the head of every\n   Python function body, increments `:depth` and raises `RecursionError`\n   through `py/raise` when the absolute depth would exceed the limit;\n   `py.sp/return`, which the stage applies to the body's value, decrements\n   it on normal exit. An escape (an exception caught above, a `return`\n(ns yang.typescript.antlr.safepoint\n  \"The `jssp` safepoint hook prelude (docs/design/yang.typescript.md\n   section 13; T1 plan section 8): `js.sp/loop` and `js.sp/call` for the\n   bundled profile and the linked `jssp` module. Universal AST, like the\n   base prelude; the `yang.safepoint` stage only places `(js.sp/loop)` and\n   `(js.sp/call)` at the `:loop` and `:call` sites the lowering marks, and\n   what they mean is written here.\n\n   Signals. The composition hands the task a signal stream, a sealed\n   reference in the store under `signals-key`; a host adapter appends one\n   plain value per delivered signal. Each hook reads it with `stream/poll!`,\n   which answers `:dao.stream/blocked` rather than parking, so a program\n   with no signal pending never waits at a safepoint. On a signal (or a\n   gap: values were lost, so at least one arrived) the hook delivers an\n   interrupt: it unwinds the handler stack to its outermost frame, the one\n   `js/run-main` installs, running every `finally` thunk on the way, and\n   throws the guest value `js.sp/interrupt` builds (an Error object named\n   `Interrupt`) through `js/throw` from there. No guest `catch` frame is\n   left to see it, so a `try`/`catch` around the loop does not catch it;\n   the run ends with it uncaught. Delivery is not journalled.\n\n   There is no depth accounting in T1: JavaScript has no RecursionError by\n   default (section 13), so `js.sp/call` is a poll only, and there is no\n   `:return` hook.\n\n   Two profiles, one source. `uast` is the bundled hook prelude: it loads\n   before the base prelude and may not touch a base definition while\n   loading, so it allocates only the signal cursor, and the hooks name base\n                                                          profile selected)\n                                 [:yin.ledger/profile :yang.site/published-set]\n                                 (:yang.site/set record))]\n        {:tree derived, :record derivation, :selected selected,\n         :record-address (jing/segment-key derivation),\n         :site-set-address (:yang.site/set record)}))))\n\n\n(defn- absent?\n  [x]\n  (= ::absent x))\n\n\n(defn- missing\n  [address]\n  {:status :missing, :address address})\n\n\n(defn- load-tree\n  \"The canonical row set `{:root :rows}` of the tree at `root` in `handle`,\n   every row fetched by its address, depth-first: `{:status :missing\n   :address a}` for the first row the handle does not hold, nil when a row\n   is not its address or no tree row.\"\n(ns yang.core.uast\n  \"Universal AST constructors shared by every language lowering and prelude. Every\n   function returns a canonical map node (`:literal`, `:variable`, `:lambda`,\n   `:application`, `:if`, `:vm/current-continuation`); nothing here adds a\n   node type.\n\n   `sexp->uast` reads a small s-expression notation into those same nodes so\n   the prelude can be written legibly:\n\n     symbol            -> :variable\n     (fn [params] b)   -> :lambda\n     (if t c a)        -> :if\n     (do a b ... z)    -> sequencing through one-parameter lambdas\n     (let [x v ...] b) -> nested immediately applied lambdas\n     (quote x)         -> :literal x\n     (%capture)        -> :vm/current-continuation\n     (yin/def k v)     -> the definition application\n     (f a ...)         -> :application\n     any other value   -> :literal\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.tails :as tails]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n\n(defn lit\n  [x]\n  {:type :literal, :value x})\n\n\n(defn v\n  [sym]\n  {:type :variable, :name sym})\n(ns yin.vm.linker.sign\n  \"Ed25519 proofs for canonical module envelopes and published head\n   traces, each under its own domain-separation prefix.\n\n   Cryptographic operations delegate to `dao.host.sign` (Slice H3):\n     `keypair-from-seed`, `sign`, `verify`.\n   String UTF-8 encoding delegates to `dao.host.text/utf8-encode`.\n   Fresh key generation (`generate`) remains here pending deferred\n   entropy design (§9.1); on jolt its `:jolt` arm draws the seed from the\n   qualified libcrypto through `yin.vm.linker.random` (the jolt-only\n   bridge over native/jolt-crypto's random entry), so entropy sits behind\n   the same provenance gate as every other crypto call.\"\n  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n            [dao.host.sign :as host-sign]\n            [dao.host.text :as text]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            #?@(:cljd [[\"package:ed25519_edwards/ed25519_edwards.dart\" :as ed]]\n                :jolt [[yin.vm.linker.random :as jolt-random]]))\n  #?@(:cljd []\n      :jolt []\n      :clj [(:import [java.security SecureRandom])]))\n\n\n(def ^:private domain \"yin.module/envelope:v1\\n\")\n\n\n;; A published head trace's prefix (yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md 5.2): domain\n;; separation, so a name envelope's signature is never a head proof and a\n;; head proof never a name envelope's.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
